+## Defect — DOM element identity destroyed by re-render
+
+The acceptance suite (Cypress, real browser) reports 5 failures, root cause in all 5:
+
+- `render()` replaces `todoList.innerHTML` with `.map(...).join('')` on every state change.
+- This destroys ALL DOM nodes inside `.todo-list` and creates new ones.
+- Cypress holds references across command chains; after the replace, those references are
+  detached from the DOM and the assertion fails.
+- The in-harness suite (happy-dom) cannot reproduce this because every step re-queries the
+  DOM fresh via `this.document.querySelector(...)`.
+
+The app-spec.md already describes the correct behaviour: "toggling the class `completed` on
+its parent `<li>`" — implying mutation, not replacement. The implementation uses
+innerHTML instead.
+
+## What was written
+
+- Added `@conformance` scenario: "The render function preserves DOM element identity" to
+  `features/todo-management.feature`. This scenario checks the source for innerHTML
+  replacement on the todo list. It is currently UNDEFINED (no step definitions exist yet).
+  When QM writes the verification, it will FAIL on the current code because the render
+  function does `todoList.innerHTML = ...`.
 
 ## Decisions
 
-- Vanilla JavaScript, no preprocessors (per spec).
-- Hash-based routing (no router library; happy-dom world.js dispatches hashchange).
-- localStorage key: `todos-vanilla`.
-- Item shape: `{ id: string, title: string, completed: boolean }`.
-- Single-file app (`js/app.js`), no controllers/models split, per simplest-sufficient-change.
+- No product scenarios were added for element identity. The existing product scenarios
+  already cover the functional behaviour (class toggling, checked state). The DOM-identity
+  requirement is a method/quality concern, pinned by the `@conformance` scenario.
+- The fix is to rewrite `render()` to mutate existing DOM nodes (toggle classList, update
+  checkbox.checked) instead of replacing innerHTML. This preserves element identity across
+  interactions.
 
